1483	/**
1484	 * ROLLBACK — a first-class, always-visible way back.
1485	 *
1486	 * The migration is a COPY. The engine connects to the old server read-only: it
1487	 * rsync-pulls files, dumps databases through root's local socket, and reads the
1488	 * live web-server config. It never writes to the source, never stops a service
1489	 * there, never edits a config there and never touches its DNS. That is the
1490	 * customer's real safety net, and it is worth nothing if they do not know it —
1491	 * before this card the only place it was ever said was one sentence in the body
1492	 * of the completion notification (`worker/migrate.ts`), which is not where
1493	 * somebody looks when their site is down.
